---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Privacy Policy", href: "/privacy-policy" }];
const updated = "24 October 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Etrynity collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website, including the contact form and Etrynity AI assistant."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-hero-inner page-hero-inner--single" style="padding-bottom:clamp(40px,5vw,64px)">
        <div class="stack">
          <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
          <h1 class="display" id="page-title" style="font-size:clamp(40px,5vw,68px)">Privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--ivory">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>This policy explains how {SITE.name} ("we", "us") handles personal information when you use this website. If you have any questions, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enquiries.</strong> When you use the contact form we receive the details you enter: your name, email address, and optionally your company, role, areas of interest and message.</li>
          <li><strong>Etrynity AI conversations.</strong> When you use the Etrynity AI assistant, Solution Finder or drafting tool, the text you type is sent to our AI provider to generate a response. This website does not store these conversations.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical information.</strong> Our hosting provider processes standard technical data, such as IP addresses and request logs, to deliver the site securely and prevent abuse.</li>
          <li id="cookies"><strong>Analytics cookies.</strong> If analytics are enabled on this site, Google Analytics cookies are set only after you choose "Accept" in the cookie banner. Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage, and you can change it at any time using "Cookie settings" in the footer.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss how we can help.</li>
          <li>To provide answers through Etrynity AI.</li>
          <li>To keep the website secure, including detecting spam and misuse.</li>
          <li>With your consent, to understand how the website is used so we can improve it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your permission.</p>

        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>We use trusted providers to run this website. They process information on our behalf and only as needed to provide their service:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — website hosting and delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of contact-form enquiries and confirmation emails.</li>
          <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — the AI model that generates Etrynity AI responses.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — website analytics, only if enabled and only with your consent.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These providers may process information in countries other than your own, under their own security and data-protection commitments.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
        <p>We keep enquiry emails for as long as needed to respond to you and manage any resulting relationship, and then delete them when they are no longer required.</p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask us to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, or object to how we use it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Please don't include sensitive personal information in the contact form or in Etrynity AI conversations.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy as our website and services evolve. The "last updated" date above shows when it was last changed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
